{"abstract":"This paper investigates the potential of applying new materialism as a frame for artistic practices to ensure multispecies perspectives in futuring initiatives. We present a case study examining artistic practices that unfolded adjacent to a construction site of an urban transformation project in Greater Copenhagen, where new residential homes are being built. As a counter-reaction to the continuous construction of new buildings without paying attention to the plurality inherent in places, our case explores how participatory, artistic, experiential, and creative formats can challenge our collective imaginations of the present and future. A growing number of researchers advocate for challenging the human-centered approaches employed in futuring and extending participation towards multispecies agency. New materialism is a theoretical and philosophical direction that foregrounds the need to consider the materiality of our world and how we, as humans, might account for our relations with nonhuman entities. By applying new materialism to artistic practices, we investigate if such practices can support multispecies futuring in the built environment. We conclude that artistic practices can 1) activate and direct attention towards the unusual in the built environment and 2) offer techniques for immersion and for shifting perspectives through anthropomorphism.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Harre, Olivia Thomassen","Holst Laursen, Lea","Andersen, Hans Jørgen","Neuhoff, Rike","Simeone, Luca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-769950"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Harre, Olivia Thomassen"],"keyword":["Artistic practice","New materialism","Urban Transformation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"framing artistic practices through new materialism to ensure multispecies futuring in the built environment","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.futures.2024.103532","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The work presented in this paper is funded by the EU project \\u2018Desire\\u2019 under the call HORIZON-MISS-2021-NEB-01-01. We want to express our deepest gratitude to the project partner NXT and Helene Johanne Christensen, the first Garden Caretaker, for inviting us into their work. The learnings and efforts from the case in Herlev feed into the broader context of the EU project Desire. Two years of experimentation were deployed in eight sites of urban transformation, and learnings and insights are being synthesized. Resources such as methods and tools will be available through the project\\u2019s website: https://www.irresistiblecircularsociety.eu/ , including narratives of the site\\u2019s sustainable futures, which will also be published here, along with other relevant resources. The work presented in this paper is funded by the Horizon Europe project \\u2018Desire\\u2019 under the call HORIZON-MISS-2021-NEB-01-01. We want to express our deepest gratitude to the project partner NXT and Helene Johanne Christensen, the first Garden Caretaker, for inviting us into their work. The learnings and efforts from the case in Herlev feed into the broader context of the EU project Desire. Two years of experimentation were deployed in eight sites of urban transformation, and learnings and insights are being synthesized. Resources such as methods and tools will be available through the project's website: https://www.irresistiblecircularsociety.eu/, including narratives of the site's sustainable futures, which will also be published here, along with other relevant resources."],"id":"S01-000.00-769950","identifier":[{"id":"85211712337","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-254cc8fe-2d85-49c4-8966-81f7c8f523a3"],"keyword":["Artistic practice","Multispecies futuring","New materialism","Urban transformation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DBF17400EDD6B2217BF76C5175F20FE0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0016328724002155?via%3Dihub","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.futures.2024.103532","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Architecture and Urban Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Urban Design – transformation & mobilities"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Olivia Thomassen","key":"harrepau","last":"Harre","locid":"4b238a51-1331-435b-8d5a-778a43447357","name":"Harre, Olivia Thomassen","orcid":"0009-0001-3681-3770","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lea","key":"holstlaursenpau","last":"Holst Laursen","locid":"1b561ecc-0f3c-447d-b0ff-a9211cb13465","name":"Holst Laursen, Lea","orcid":"0000-0001-5139-5282","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Jørgen","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"7ba27faa-e069-404b-8502-76309dad24a3","name":"Andersen, Hans Jørgen