{"abstract":"Report that outlines the first learnings from applying the Desire principles and tools in demonstration activities at each of the eight territorial sites, as well as reflections on future plans","author_count":4,"contributors":["Neuhoff, Rike","Harre, Olivia Thomassen","Andersen, Hans Jørgen","Holst Laursen, Lea"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-769913"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"desire site experiences and future plans d 000000000003 000000000002","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"doo","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-769913","ids":["aau-1ffbb4c4-c753-4ece-9372-d99dc8aa13ae"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-22485A64223DCA1E72E38A20028DA8CD"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Copenhagen","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Service Systems Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rike","key":"neuhoffpau","last":"Neuhoff","locid":"2c453c44-1cb3-4875-92d7-5005eb289729","name":"Neuhoff, Rike","orcid":"0000-0002-2448-1844","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Olivia Thomassen","key":"harrepau","last":"Harre","locid":"4b238a51-1331-435b-8d5a-778a43447357","name":"Harre, Olivia Thomassen","orcid":"0009-0001-3681-3770","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Jørgen","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"7ba27faa-e069-404b-8502-76309dad24a3","name":"Andersen, Hans Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-0940-0698","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lea","key":"holstlaursenpau","last":"Holst Laursen","locid":"1b561ecc-0f3c-447d-b0ff-a9211cb13465","name":"Holst Laursen, Lea","orcid":"0000-0001-5139-5282","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"u"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Unpublished"]},"sid":["aau-1ffbb4c4-c753-4ece-9372-d99dc8aa13ae"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Desire site experiences and future plans (D. 3.2)","type":"Other-Unknown","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-769913","year":"2024","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The narratives represent a practice-based perspective of the project’s two-year outcomes, focusing on actions carried out by eight urban sites of transformation. Driven by forming, shaping, and organising activities in the urban transformation projects, eight sites have experimented with interpreting and translating the values of New European Bauhaus and five Desire principles (Biodiversity, Belonging, Movement, Circularity, Aesthetics). The narratives unfold the intricacies and nuances of running place-based activities and experiences, putting words and images into understanding their place, processes, dynamics, and potential futures.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Harre, Olivia Thomassen","Carstens, Asbjørn Christian","Hermansen, Daniel Knud","Holst Laursen, Lea","Andersen, Hans Jørgen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-771305"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"narratives of irresistible circular futures","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/757423602/Whitepaper_Endelig_19_12_2024_v_1.2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The work presented in this paper is funded by the EU project 'Desire - Designing the Irresistible Circular Society' under the call HORIZON-MISS-2021-NEB-01-01"],"id":"S01-000.00-771305","ids":["aau-ed3cf8f8-d159-4824-8f81-f984599ffd26"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B2274F92B373F8AA0CDD7FA127F82F61"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/757423602/Whitepaper_Endelig_19_12_2024_v_1.2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Architecture and Urban Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Urban Design – transformation & mobilities"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Olivia Thomassen","key":"harrepau","last":"Harre","locid":"4b238a51-1331-435b-8d5a-778a43447357","name":"Harre, Olivia Thomassen","orcid":"0009-0001-3681-3770","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Asbjørn Christian","key":"carstenspau","last":"Carstens","locid":"ff0aafa6-1e78-429d-993a-999a953bea18","name":"Carstens, Asbjørn Christian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel Knud","key":"hermansenpau","last":"Hermansen","locid":"1b0cfc92-d26e-40d4-8348-9df84f697ffd","name":"Hermansen, Daniel Knud","orcid":"0009-0006-4820-5437","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lea","key":"holstlaursenpau","last":"Holst Laursen","locid":"1b561ecc-0f3c-447d-b0ff-a9211cb13465","name":"Holst Laursen, Lea","orcid":"0000-0001-5139-5282","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Jørgen","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"7ba27faa-e069-404b-8502-76309dad24a3","name":"Andersen, Hans Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-0940-0698","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"142","place":"Aalborg","publisher":"Department of Architecture and Design, Aalborg University","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ed3cf8f8-d159-4824-8f81-f984599ffd26"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Narratives of Irresistible Circular Futures","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-771305","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In this chapter, the authors argue that when service design is introduced into an organization, it is not only the product that is transformed, but also the organization itself. The authors use the term \"material\" to refer to \"that which is being changed\" and in this case, it is the organization. The authors draw on their own experiences as design researchers in an organization and combine them with insights from interviews with professional designers and managers to understand the involvement of professional designers and the applied design methods in IT development projects. They argue that the introduction and use of service design artefacts initiates a change in the material, the organization, and explore how these artefacts not only orchestrate a service experience but also support a change in mindset and focus that influences the organization. They show how artefacts simultaneously represent the present 'what is' and propose a future 'what could become' through three distinct but interrelated stages: collecting, abstracting, selecting, and reframing, and anchoring, presenting, and awakening.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Harre, Olivia Thomassen","Nielsen, Lene"],"cuid":["S02-090.08-724181"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Organisational aspects","Service Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"organisations as material","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/en/publications/6a02de30-9b4e-437b-9593-6dc2c3fd66c5","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-090.08-724181","identifier":[{"id":"85192736730","type":"scopus"},{"id":"85192725082","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-6a02de30-9b4e-437b-9593-6dc2c3fd66c5","itu-fed21b0d-8231-40e9-8329-ea7b5f034ed8"],"keyword":["organisational aspects","service design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-4-38C133DEAB192D432B9C38859E6C715F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Architecture and Urban Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, REFLACT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Olivia Thomassen","key":"harrepau","last":"Harre","locid":"4b238a51-1331-435b-8d5a-778a43447357","name":"Harre, Olivia Thomassen","orcid":"0009-0001-3681-3770","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Johan","key":"blomkvistpedh","last":"Blomkvist","name":"Blomkvist, Johan","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Johan","key":"blomquistpedh","last":"Blomquist","name":"Blomquist, Johan","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Simon","key":"clatworthypedh","last":"Clatworthy","name":"Clatworthy, Simon","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Stefan","key":"holmlidpedh","last":"Holmlid","name":"Holmlid, Stefan","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4337/9781802203301","eisbn":["9781802203301"],"isbn":["9781802203295"],"pages":"95-100","publisher":"Edward Elgar Publishing","status":"p","title":"The Materials of Service Design"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85192736730"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6a02de30-9b4e-437b-9593-6dc2c3fd66c5","itu-fed21b0d-8231-40e9-8329-ea7b5f034ed8"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Organisations as material","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-090.08-724181","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This reflective paper proposes a research agenda that investigates and questions how and if we need to assess the service design tools and their usability in the context of organisations’ design maturity. Maps and tool in the service design toolbox are perceived as straightforward by some organisations, however for organisations with low service design maturity such tools can pose challenges in how to utilise and leverage their potential. As a direction for future studies, this research agenda sheds light on how common service design tools are affected by organisational usability and maturity.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene","Harre, Olivia Thomassen","Abdelnour-Nocera, Jose","Li, Christina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-692467"],"event":{"end":"2023-07-14","place":"Rio De Janeiro, br","start":"2023-07-11","title":"ServDes 2023","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Infinite Interactive LTD","University of West London"],"keyword":["Organisational design maturity","Service Design","Tools","Usability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"proposing organisational usability as an enabler of organisational service design maturity","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3384/ecp203039","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-692467","ids":["aau-1f1e4387-32d5-40ea-afcc-47f2b4cbaa25"],"keyword":["Service Design","organisational design maturity","tools","usability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["